{"id":"64b5bf078722d744","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-iid.md","title":"Independent Identically Distributed","display":"df-iid — Independent Identically Distributed","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-iid","aliases":["58-df-iid","Independent Identically Distributed","i.i.d."],"display":"df-iid — Independent Identically Distributed","depends_on":["[[../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-iid"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-iid</span><span>Independent Identically Distributed</span><span>i.i.d.</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-iid — Independent Identically Distributed"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"49ad0501f11b0cd1\" href=\"?note=49ad0501f11b0cd1\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md\">../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\((\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (probability space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,\\mathcal E)\">\\((E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (measurable state space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\neq\\emptyset\">\\(I\\neq\\emptyset\\)</span> (index set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\in(E^\\Omega)^I\">\\(X\\in(E^\\Omega)^I\\)</span> (family <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i\\mapsto X_i\">\\(i\\mapsto X_i\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (probability measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,\\mathcal E)\">\\((E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}_S\\)</span> (upstream predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IID}_S(X,I,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\">\\(\\mathrm{IID}_S(X,I,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (i.i.d.-family predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}iid} \\vdash \\mathrm{IID}_S(X,I,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E) \\leftrightarrow I\\neq\\emptyset\\land X\\in(E^\\Omega)^I\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\mathbb P(\\Omega)=1\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mu(E)=1\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S(X_i;(\\Omega,\\mathcal F),(E,\\mathcal E))\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal E\\;(\\mathbb P(X_i^{-1}[A])=\\mu(A))\\Bigr)\\land\\forall J\\subseteq I\\;\\Bigl((J\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Finite}_S(J))\\to\\forall B\\in\\mathcal E^J\\;(\\mathbb P(\\bigcap_{j\\in J}X_j^{-1}[B(j)])=\\prod_{j\\in J}\\mu(B(j)))\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}iid} \\vdash \\mathrm{IID}_S(X,I,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E) \\leftrightarrow I\\neq\\emptyset\\land X\\in(E^\\Omega)^I\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\mathbb P(\\Omega)=1\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mu(E)=1\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S(X_i;(\\Omega,\\mathcal F),(E,\\mathcal E))\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal E\\;(\\mathbb P(X_i^{-1}[A])=\\mu(A))\\Bigr)\\land\\forall J\\subseteq I\\;\\Bigl((J\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Finite}_S(J))\\to\\forall B\\in\\mathcal E^J\\;(\\mathbb P(\\bigcap_{j\\in J}X_j^{-1}[B(j)])=\\prod_{j\\in J}\\mu(B(j)))\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>i.i.d.: same law, independent</li>\n<li>Pairwise independence is weaker than the finite-subfamily independence used in the definition.</li>\n<li>Means, variances, and laws of large numbers require integrability assumptions and are not consequences of i.i.d. alone.</li>\n<li>WLLN: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar{X}_n \\to \\mu\">\\(\\bar{X}_n \\to \\mu\\)</span> in probability</li>\n<li>SLLN: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar{X}_n \\to \\mu\">\\(\\bar{X}_n \\to \\mu\\)</span> almost surely</li>\n<li>CLT: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)/\\sigma \\to N(0,1)\">\\(\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)/\\sigma \\to N(0,1)\\)</span> in distribution</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md","status":"resolved","id":"49ad0501f11b0cd1","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-finite.md","status":"resolved","id":"d9a25b0ac94a3598","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"(E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"I\\neq\\emptyset","display":false},{"tex":"X\\in(E^\\Omega)^I","display":false},{"tex":"i\\mapsto X_i","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"(E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Finite}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{IID}_S(X,I,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}iid} \\vdash \\mathrm{IID}_S(X,I,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E) \\leftrightarrow I\\neq\\emptyset\\land X\\in(E^\\Omega)^I\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\mathbb P(\\Omega)=1\\land\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mu(E)=1\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S(X_i;(\\Omega,\\mathcal F),(E,\\mathcal E))\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal E\\;(\\mathbb P(X_i^{-1}[A])=\\mu(A))\\Bigr)\\land\\forall J\\subseteq I\\;\\Bigl((J\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Finite}_S(J))\\to\\forall B\\in\\mathcal E^J\\;(\\mathbb P(\\bigcap_{j\\in J}X_j^{-1}[B(j)])=\\prod_{j\\in J}\\mu(B(j)))\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\bar{X}_n \\to \\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar{X}_n \\to \\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)/\\sigma \\to N(0,1)","display":false}],"bytes":2003,"backlinks":[{"id":"b01b13e1ea3167d2","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{IID}_S(X,\\mathbb N_{>0},\\nu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))$，即 $(X(n))_{n\\geq1}$ 是共同分布为 $\\nu$ 的独立同分布实随机变量（see [[../batch07/58-df-iid.md]]）"},{"id":"e13c87067d559828","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)$ (i.i.d. predicate, see [[58-df-iid]])"},{"id":"1615e311b8c1eba3","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"9df3239945c5331e","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"4932fa2e649322cf","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{IID}_S\\subseteq V^8$ (see [[../batch07/58-df-iid.md]])."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-659","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-iid.md|58-df-iid]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["49ad0501f11b0cd1","ca832ed6bc22f728","d9a25b0ac94a3598"]}